Generic single-database configuration for KasirKu.

## Common commands

    # Create a new revision from model changes
    cd backend && alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add column X"

    # Apply pending migrations
    cd backend && alembic upgrade head

    # Rollback last migration
    cd backend && alembic downgrade -1

    # Mark current DB as up-to-date (no schema change) — useful when
    # bootstrapping alembic on a database that already has tables.
    cd backend && alembic stamp head

## Notes
- `env.py` reads `DATABASE_URL` from `backend/.env` (asyncpg driver).
- `Base` is imported from `server.py` so all models are auto-discovered.
- `compare_type=True` is enabled for accurate diffs on autogenerate.
